abstract: >-
  Python software layer for a private Meshtastic LoRa mesh network used as a backup channel
  for critical logistics operations of small and medium-sized enterprises. A gateway collector
  records packet (L1), device (L2) and logistics-event (L3) metadata into a local SQLite store
  without Internet access; a compact 24-byte binary protocol on PRIVATE_APP (port 256) carries
  EVENT/ACCEPT/DONE messages; kpi.py computes the indicators of the accompanying article
  (channel utilization, delivery ratio, age of information, actionability eta, operational
  autonomy A_op, loss reduction R_loss). A synthetic replay generator allows reproduction
  without radio hardware. Verified on synthetic data only, not on field measurements.
keywords:
  - Meshtastic
  - LoRa
  - mesh network
  - SME logistics
  - supply chain resilience
  - business continuity
  - operational autonomy
  - age of information
  - metadata collection
  - SQLite
